# MEMORY.md - Long-Term Memory

## Data Storage
- All data in `data/` folder (JSON files)
- Company: `data/companies/{{COMPANY_CODE}}/`
- Candidates: `data/candidates/{PHONE}/`
- Employees: `data/companies/{{COMPANY_CODE}}/employees/{PHONE}/`
- Positions: `data/companies/{{COMPANY_CODE}}/positions/{POSITION_CODE}.json`
- Shifts: `data/companies/{{COMPANY_CODE}}/shifts/`
- Attendance: `data/companies/{{COMPANY_CODE}}/attendance/`
- Leave: `data/companies/{{COMPANY_CODE}}/leave/`
- Payroll: `data/companies/{{COMPANY_CODE}}/payroll/`

## Current Setup
- Company: {{COMPANY_NAME}} (code: {{COMPANY_CODE}})
- Country: {{COUNTRY_CODE}}
- Enabled modules: {{MODULES_LIST}}
- Positions live in `data/companies/{{COMPANY_CODE}}/positions/*.json`
- Current active openings must be read from the live position JSON files
{{#MODULE_SHIFTS}}
- Shift schedules are operational records keyed by employee and date
- Employees may only ask about their own shifts
- Availability and shift swap requests are operational records tied to employee phone identity and manager scope
{{/MODULE_SHIFTS}}
{{#MODULE_ATTENDANCE}}
- Attendance records are operational records keyed by employee, date, and shift
- Employees may only check in/out or ask about their own attendance
- Vague attendance follow-ups require scoped pending operation state before changing records
{{/MODULE_ATTENDANCE}}
{{#MODULE_LEAVE}}
- Leave requests are operational records keyed by employee and date range
- Approved leave blocks unsafe absence marking for the same employee/date
{{/MODULE_LEAVE}}
{{#MODULE_PAYROLL}}
- Payroll Hours is a read-only calculation layer over Shifts, Attendance, and approved Leave
- Timesheet approvals freeze reviewed payroll-hour snapshots by employee and period
- Payroll Policy controls previews for leave, overtime, deductions, and optional hourly rate
- Payroll Export locks approved preview snapshots for explicit periods
- Employees may only see their own payroll hours and timesheet status, bound by sender phone
- Do not process payments, bank files, or transfers; payroll preview/export only
{{/MODULE_PAYROLL}}
{{#MODULE_ANALYTICS}}
- Analytics is a read-only insight layer over Shifts, Attendance, Leave, Availability, Shift Swaps, Payroll Hours, and Timesheets
- Analytics respects branch/team manager scope and updates dashboards only for company-wide HR views
{{/MODULE_ANALYTICS}}

## Scope and Routing
- Phone number in `hr-users.json` decides HR vs candidate/employee mode
- Optional branch/team manager scopes restrict HR-mode users to assigned employees and operational records
- Greeting-only candidate openers may get one onboarding reply asking for `APPLY-{{COMPANY_CODE}}-{POSITION_CODE}`
- Out-of-scope candidate messages return `NO_REPLY`
- Out-of-scope HR messages return `I can only help with HR-related tasks. 📋`

## Apply Links
- Build apply links dynamically as:
- `https://wa.me/{{WHATSAPP_NUMBER_PLAIN}}?text=APPLY-{{COMPANY_CODE}}-{POSITION_CODE}`

## Google Sheets Dashboard
- Sheet ID: `{{SHEET_ID}}`
- URL: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/{{SHEET_ID}}/edit
- Use `--values-json` for all writes
- Column S stores `APPKEY:{PHONE}-{COMPANY}-{POSITION}` for idempotency

## Language Rules
- Match the user's dominant language
- One language per message only
- Do not mix Arabic and English except unavoidable technical terms like CV, PDF, or QR
